("730","Receptionist : Hello Sir, good evening! May I help you?
\nMr. Ryefield : Yes, please. I have a reservation in my name: James Ryefield.
\nReceptionist : Sorry Sir, can you spell your last name, please?
\nMr. Ryefield : That’s R-Y-E-F-I-E-L-D.
\nReceptionist : Thank you Sir. Have you got your ID, please?
\nMr. Ryefield : Oh! God! I have forgotten it in the car!
\nReceptionist : No problem Sir. We’ll make a copy later. What’s your address and
\nphone number, please?
\nMr. Ryefield : 36 Mable Road, Liverpool, and my phone number is 7025581439.
\nReceptionist : If you don’t mind Sir, I would like to make you a few more questions,
\nbecause we are doing a statistic on our guests.
\nMr. Ryefield : OK. Go ahead!
\nReceptionist : What’s your job?
\nMr. Ryefield : I’m a journalist.
\nReceptionist : Where and when were you born?
\nMr. Ryefield : I was born in South Africa on October 6th 1973.
\nReceptionist : Is this your first time in our hotel?
\nMr. Ryefield : Yes, it is. A friend of mine usually stays here and advised me.
\nReceptionist : Thanks for your time! Your room number is 28, on the 2nd floor. The lift is just on your left. Enjoy your stay!
\nMr. Ryefield : Thanks! One more thing, what time do you serve breakfast?
\nReceptionist : From 8 until 11 am. Have a good night, Sir!
\nMr. Ryefield : Thanks! Likewise!
