("15445","1636","912","1360,1361,1362,1363,1364,1365,1366,1367,1368,1369","Signs or symbols (Symbolism) resulting from related graphic design, such as symbols and marks. that helps create a unique identity for products and services for companies, stores, organizations or manufacturers|=>Signs or symbols (Symbolism) resulting from related graphic design, such as symbols and marks. that helps create a unique identity for products and services for companies, stores, organizations or manufacturers|=>Monthly and daily employees who are employed on temporary or scheduled employment, however, the employment period cannot exceed a fiscal year. Employee type|=>Valentine\'s Day, also called Saint Valentine\'s Day or the Feast of Saint Valentine,[1] is celebrated annually on February 14.[2] It originated as a Christian feast day honoring one or two early Christian martyrs named Saint Valentine and, through later folk traditions, has become a significant cultural, religious, and commercial celebration of romance and love in many regions of the world.[3]|=>confused|=>confused|=>confused|=>confused|=>The three main colors in the flag are red, white and navy blue. The interior is divided into 5 stripes, the innermost bar is blue. Next to the outside, both the top and bottom are white and red respectively. The blue band is twice the size of the other bands. The significance of the tricolor flag refers to the three main institutions of Thailand, namely the nation (red), religion (white), and the king (blue). is the origin of the name of this flag as the tricolor flag (tri = three, chromatic = color)|=>77 provinces","","","1"),
