\nJuly 20, (2021)
\nKing Transportation lines 188-192 Williams Street
\n 
\n Providence 7, Rhode Island Gentlemen:
\nThis letter is typed in the Block Style. The date line is typed to end with the right margin of the letter. That date line could also be centered under the letterhead design.
\nThe mixed style of punctuation is used. There is no period after the date line. There are no
\nMarks of punctuation at the end of the lines in the address. A comma, however, separates The zone number from the state name.
\nThe salutation is followed by a colon. A comma is typed at the end of the complimentary Close. Notice, however, that there are no punctuation marks after the company name and the salutation is followed by colon. A comma is typed at the end of the complimentary close. Notice, however, that there are no punctuation marks after the company name and the official title. Each line of the address, as well as each line in the body of the letter begins at the left writing margin. The three lines in the conclusion are blocked and centered. The identifying initials-the initials of the dictator and of the stenographer-are usually typed two single line spaces below the title, as in this letter.
\nThe Block Style is economical of time. Some business men, however, consider it radical because the paragraphs are not indented.
