\nThis letter is typed in the Block Style. the date line is typed to end with the right nargin of the letter. That date line could also be centered under the letthrhead design. 
\nThe mixed style of punctuation is used. There is no penod after the date line. There are no marks of punctuation at the end of the lines in the addressee. A comma, how ever, separates the zone number from the state name 
\nThe salutation is followed by a colon. A comma is typed at the end of the complimentary close. Notice, however, that there are no punctuation marks after company name and the official title. Each line of the address, as well as each line in the body of the letter begins at the laft writing margin. The three lines in the conclusion are blocked and centered.
\nThe identifying initials-the initials of the dictator and of the stenographer-are usually typed two single line spaces below the title, as in this letter.
\nThe Block Style is economical of time. Some     business men, however, consider if radical because the paragraphs are not interested.
\n
